# Binary files git must never touch.
#
# Without this, core.autocrlf on Windows treats a PDF or an image as text and
# rewrites every 0x0A byte in it on checkout. `git add` warned about exactly
# that for the user manual: "LF will be replaced by CRLF". The file would have
# been committed intact and come back corrupt on the next clone.
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.aab   binary
*.apk   binary
*.keystore binary
*.jks   binary
*.db    binary
